@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: why `proveo run opencode` can stop taking keys, and which hop ate them
' covers: internal/ptyproxy/inputfilter.go
' covers: internal/ptyproxy/inputfilter_test.go
' covers: internal/ptyproxy/ptyproxy.go
' covers: internal/ptyproxy/ptyproxy_test.go
' covers: internal/backend/sandbox/sandbox.go
'   the filter this sits on ........ _spec/internal/ptyproxy/terminal-report-filter.puml
'   who owns the PTY ............... _spec/internal/ptyproxy/pty-ownership.puml
' Notes are capped at 5 lines x 50 columns; one idea per anchor.

title OpenCode keyboard stall — two proveo hops, then the rest

actor "Operator" as OP

node "proveo ptyproxy" as PX <<host>> {
  component "held private CSI\n""ESC[?62;"" + letter" as HOLD <<error>>
  component "DropReports\ncredits per query class" as CRED <<app>>
  component "stdin pump\nreal tty → master" as IN <<app>>
}

node "sbx run opencode" as SBX <<cloud>> {
  component "OpenTUI native\nqueryTerminalSend" as QT <<app>>
}

component "OpenCode TUI" as OC <<app>>
component "kitty CSI-u keys\nwith parser still off" as KITTY <<error>>
component "upstream Enter swallow\n#31217 · #8229 · 1.18.x" as UP <<error>>

OP ARROW_MAIN IN : keystrokes · DA · CSI ? Nu
IN ARROW_ERROR HOLD : letter becomes CSI final
IN ARROW_MAIN CRED
CRED ARROW_MAIN SBX : keystrokes + owed replies
SBX ARROW_MAIN QT : ""CSI ? u"" · ""CSI >0q"" · DECRQM · DA1
QT ARROW_MAIN OC
CRED ARROW_ERROR KITTY : query answer dropped
OC ARROW_OPTIONAL UP : after first reply

note bottom of HOLD
  **A split DA is not an arrow key.** Held
  ""ESC[?62;"" plus the next letter made
  ""ESC[?62;h"" — complete CSI, final h,
  ""reportNone"", and the letter never
  reached the prompt. Window: 2s.
end note

note top of CRED
  **CPR was the first class, not the
  only one.** OpenTUI asks on output
  for kitty flags, XTVERSION, DA1 and
  DECRPM. DropReports ate those too,
  so detection ran deaf.
end note

note bottom of QT
  **Negotiation is native, not JS.**
  ""CSI ? u"" then, if answered,
  ""CSI >5u"" (push). No answer: the
  parser never sets kitty mode.
end note

note right of KITTY
  **Kitty sends CSI-u by default.**
  OpenTUI only defers split CSI-u
  when ""kittyKeyboardEnabled"".
  Query silence + Kitty term =
  keys that vanish.
end note

note as N_TRACE
  **Measure, do not guess.**
  ""PROVEO_TRACE_STDIN"" is the
  verdict log: sent vs DROPPED,
  including the held stump.
end note

note as N_UPSTREAM
  **Idle freeze was this hook.**
  git-sync cat'd the TTY at
  session.idle (a1e4a36). Enter
  swallow after a turn (#31217)
  is a separate OpenCode bug.
end note

note as N_FILTER_OFF
  **A/B.** ""PROVEO_STDIN_FILTER=off""
  restores passthrough. If keys
  return, the filter is the hop.
  If they do not, look upstream.
end note
@enduml
